                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "231474802",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198367471798",
                            "num_reviews": 30072,
                            "playtime_forever": 653,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 653,
                            "last_played": 1785187937
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Developed and published by Sure Games, By Any Means Necessary is a turn-based role-playing game that embraces the spirit of classic RPGs while introducing several mechanics that encourage a more strategic approach to combat. The story begins after the sudden appearance of a mysterious portal that releases monsters across the world, pushing long-standing rival nations into an uneasy alliance. Players take control of Captain Yusef Athros of the Sylon Empire, who is dispatched to Lavinan Island to investigate the growing crisis. While the narrative follows a familiar fantasy formula of uncovering the source of an otherworldly threat, it provides enough intrigue and world-building to motivate exploration and carry players through the adventure.\n\nCombat is where the game establishes its identity. Instead of allowing players to rely on healing items or restorative consumables during battles, it forces them to think carefully about every action. Success depends on understanding party abilities, managing resources efficiently, and making smart tactical decisions rather than simply recovering health whenever things become difficult. This design choice makes even routine encounters feel more deliberate and rewarding. An additional bonus action system further enriches battles by granting extra opportunities when certain conditions are fulfilled, encouraging experimentation with different strategies and party combinations. These mechanics give combat a satisfying layer of depth that separates it from many traditional retro-inspired RPGs.\n\nCharacter growth is equally engaging thanks to a progression system centered around collectible scrolls. Rather than limiting advancement to gaining levels, players can use these scrolls to improve attributes and unlock new skills that shape each character into a specialized role. Whether building a resilient defender, a powerful damage dealer, or a versatile support unit, the customization offers meaningful flexibility without becoming unnecessarily complicated. The progression feels steady throughout the campaign, rewarding exploration and thoughtful planning while keeping the mechanics accessible to both newcomers and longtime RPG enthusiasts.\n\nBeyond the main storyline, the game encourages players to explore optional content that expands both its gameplay and replay value. Numerous side quests, hidden areas, optional dungeons, and special activities such as hunting powerful monsters in the Norsfolk Swamp or competing in the Pet Arena provide welcome variety. Searching for the strongest scrolls and uncovering hidden rewards gives players an incentive to thoroughly investigate every location instead of rushing toward the ending. These optional objectives help make the world feel more rewarding and provide worthwhile challenges for those seeking additional content beyond the central campaign.\n\nThe presentation remains faithful to its retro inspirations with colorful pixel art, straightforward animations, and a clean interface that prioritizes functionality over visual spectacle. While the graphics are intentionally modest, they effectively capture the nostalgic charm of classic role-playing games without feeling outdated. The soundtrack and overall atmosphere complement the adventure well, creating an experience that values gameplay and strategic depth over technical ambition. Although players expecting modern production values may find the presentation simplistic, those who appreciate old-school RPG aesthetics will likely find its visual style appealing.\n\nBy Any Means Necessary succeeds because it understands exactly what kind of experience it wants to deliver. Rather than attempting to compete with larger RPGs through scale or cinematic presentation, it focuses on building satisfying tactical combat, rewarding progression, and meaningful optional content. The restrictions placed on battle recovery, combined with the bonus action system and character customization, create encounters that remain engaging from beginning to end. Although the story follows familiar fantasy themes and the visuals stay comfortably within retro conventions, the gameplay offers enough originality to make the adventure memorable for fans of classic turn-based role-playing games.\n\nRating: 6/10",
